# The OFFSITE restic repository on Backblaze B2, plus the copy direction:
# RESTIC_REPOSITORY is the destination (B2) and RESTIC_FROM_REPOSITORY the
# source (the local repo), so `restic copy` needs no flags — the same env
# file drives copy, forget and check against the offsite side.
#
# The repository URL lives in the VAULT (field `repository` on the
# `restic-b2` item) rather than here, because its region segment only
# exists once the B2 account does — connection details originate in the
# vault, same as garage/rclone.env. Both repos share one password
# deliberately: they fall to the same vault compromise either way, and a
# second item would just be a second thing to lose.
RESTIC_REPOSITORY="op://Wolfe.Lab/restic-b2/repository"
RESTIC_PASSWORD="op://Wolfe.Lab/restic-repo/password"
RESTIC_FROM_REPOSITORY=/Volumes/Data2/restic
RESTIC_FROM_PASSWORD="op://Wolfe.Lab/restic-repo/password"
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="op://Wolfe.Lab/restic-b2/username"
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="op://Wolfe.Lab/restic-b2/credential"
